You can modify the pattern string in the `SimpleDateFormat` to include the week number and month abbreviation, then add prefixes and suffixes to the result to match the desired format. Here's an example implementation:

```
fun currentWeek(): String {
    // Get week number and month abbreviation
    val weekNum = currentDate[Calendar.WEEK_OF_YEAR]
    val month = currentDate[Calendar.MONTH]
    val monthAbbr = DateFormatSymbols(Locale.getDefault()).shortMonths[month]

    // Build date format and format current date
    val dateFormat = SimpleDateFormat("w_${monthAbbr}_yyyy", Locale.getDefault())
    val formattedDate = dateFormat.format(currentDate.time)

    // Add prefix and suffix to formatted date
    return "Week_$formattedDate"
}
```

In this code, we first get the week number and month abbreviation using the `Calendar` and `DateFormatSymbols` APIs. We then build the date format string in the pattern "w_MMM_yyyy" and format the current date using `SimpleDateFormat`. Finally, we add the "Week_" prefix to the formatted date and return the result.

